"answer": "Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) causes pain, swelling, and stiffness in joints by attacking the lining of the joints and damaging the tissue covering the ends of bones, which can eventually impair joint function [MLP-1232]. Inflammation from RA can also affect other body parts, including the eyes, skin, heart, nerves, blood, and lungs [MLP-1232]."
}
